    "complexity_is_proportional": false,
    "rationale": "Rejected and removed. The bit-exact prototype reduced each eligible per-level interleave/9/7 sequence from 11 physical dispatches to 3, but resident end-to-end improvement was only 0.34-1.57% and host readback crossed no-change (-2.65% to +0.05%). The design consumed 16 KiB of threadgroup memory and fell back beyond 4096 samples instead of providing the required tiled-halo long-axis path. Vendor occupancy, register, private-memory, spill, and cache evidence was unavailable, so the small result does not justify production complexity."
